Subject: Its manifest standalone, as crates.io's package states it
Why: aws-lc-rs's manifest in its repository inherits from that repository's workspace (versions, lints) and takes aws-lc-sys and aws-lc-fips-sys by path, from folders kiln doesn't vendor (aws-lc-sys's AWS-LC sources are a submodule). crates.io's package of the same release (1.18.2) states it standalone, its dependencies by version: kiln takes that manifest, as kiln took the crate from crates.io before, so aws-lc-sys stays crates.io's 0.46.0.

